manuscripts.abstract:
We prove the sixth-symmetric-power case of Foulkes' conjecture. For every integer *b* ≥ 6 and every finite-dimensional complex vector space *V*, there is a $\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}
olimits (V)$-equivariant injection $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)\hookrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6 V)$.

For every finite-dimensional complex vector space *V*, we prove that the canonical Foulkes–Howe map $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a V)\longrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)$ is surjective whenever *a* ≥ 2 and $b\ge a(a-1)$. This gives a quadratic stabilization bound independent of $\dim V$.
